      {
        "id": "p22-ex19e-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\sin\\theta=\\cos\\theta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=45^\\circ,\\ 225^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "When $\\cos\\theta=0$, the original equation is not satisfied, so divide by $\\cos\\theta$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}&=1\\\\\\tan\\theta&=1\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe related angle is $45^\\circ$. Tangent is positive in the first and third quadrants.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=45^\\circ\\text{ or }180^\\circ+45^\\circ\\\\\\theta&=45^\\circ\\text{ or }225^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-ex19e-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\sqrt{3}\\cos\\theta-\\sin\\theta=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=60^\\circ,\\ 240^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\sin\\theta&=\\sqrt{3}\\cos\\theta\\end{align*}$$\n\nWhen $\\cos\\theta=0$, the original equation is not satisfied, so divide by $\\cos\\theta$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}&=\\sqrt{3}\\\\\\tan\\theta&=\\sqrt{3}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe related angle is $60^\\circ$. Tangent is positive in the first and third quadrants.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=60^\\circ\\text{ or }180^\\circ+60^\\circ\\\\\\theta&=60^\\circ\\text{ or }240^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      }
    ]
